                        "sense_id": "34c8e16a-9520-373e-b3e0-8d6fa09a830d",
                        "entry_id": "1c03061b-df0c-3020-8e02-ee5888c91f98",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Illuminated by sunlight."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "123cec48-c3f9-4ba9-9d7f-a896d11ea5a7",
                                "sense_id": "34c8e16a-9520-373e-b3e0-8d6fa09a830d",
                                "text": "With something, consequently, of the feeling which thrill the exile as he looks, for the last time, on the country of his birth, or with which the dying gaze on the sunlighted earth from whence they know their spirit is departing, Vanda looked back upon the misty heights of Jagodina, till leaving the banks of the bright Morawa, along which, for a time, their course lay, they plunged into the mighty forests, through which ran the road to Rudnik, and the feathery crowns of the ancient trees gradually hid Jagodina from her sight, and the last faint trace of its loftiest peak became blended with the white clouds of the summer sky."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93bb670e-8ffe-4389-a454-e2244de97931",
                                "sense_id": "34c8e16a-9520-373e-b3e0-8d6fa09a830d",
                                "text": "The point of light in the right one is the reflection, on the under part of the ball, of the light from the nose, which could, of course, be seen on the sunlighted side only."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7e67453-df4a-4ab0-a600-0b4284369be9",
                                "sense_id": "34c8e16a-9520-373e-b3e0-8d6fa09a830d",
                                "text": "I have come to learn, or perhaps I have forced myself to believe, these doldrum days will be followed by a day, or a few hours, of euphoria in which the mind, tired of its own torment, races off to dance in some sunlighted field."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
